oss the memory holds.","close":"commit closes the session; an uncommitted session is not part of the memory.","form":"Write each fact as one sentence: 「X の Y は A」 (X the whole subject, Y what is asked about, A a noun phrase) or an event 「X が Y を V」; a change as 「Y は A から B に変更」 or 「Y は B に更新」. One fact per sentence.","frozen":"Every cross a write made is frozen: unseat swap extend topic set_depth link unlink drop -> memory_frozen. add / open_cross / seat / emit are not tools of a memory session.","history":"A write is judged against the sentences BEFORE it, never against itself (REVERSAL / NEW_RELATION / UNANCHORED); notes never block.","keep_unshaped":"keep_unshaped(text, role) stores a sentence that has no shape (the F0 tank): it is in the memory and can be searched as text, it enters no cross and fires no note. Refused (shaped) if every clause has a shape: use write.","output":"A memory session never emits: its only product is the sentences it writes. Plain text is discarded unread.","recall":"recall(question) reads the question with the same shape exchanger as a write and answers from the CROSSES: ANSWER (one value), UPDATED (the latest value + `history`), CHOICE (two or more values at one place: nothing is ranked), NONE (`issues` say why). Every value comes with the sentence that wrote it (`sid`, `span`): quote that stretch and emit.","report":"report(contradictions, bugs) ends EVERY turn: contradictions = pairs of turn ids (\"1-3\" = session 1, message 3) whose statements disagree, [] if none; bugs = [] here. A REVERSAL note names the two sentences it is about (`sentence`, `earlier`, and `cite`: the turn pairs you can report).","supersede":"A write whose value differs from an earlier value at the SAME place (the same Y of the same X, in the same nest) shows a SAME_SEAT note, a change clause an UPDATE note, a pair of phrases in opposite roles a REVERSAL_X note, another owner of the same attribute an ENUMERATION note (information only); each names the sentences 